{
  "name": "name-literal-confidence",
  "description": "A package-level declaration whose name a string literal of a production file spells, outside the declaration itself, is reported at the class possible under each candidate and visibility code, with the literal's position in the finding's details, because a tool reading the source may find the declaration by that name. A method of a type is a declaration of its own, so a literal in its body lowers the type, and so is each specification of a grouped declaration, so a literal in one lowers a sibling the group declares. The same declaration is certain where only a test file or its own declaration spells the name. A declaration only a lowered declaration reaches keeps the class certain at the confidence possible, because it falls in that declaration's component. An import path, a struct tag and a struct field's name lower nothing.",
  "languages": [
    "go"
  ],
  "target_kind": "application",
  "closed_world": [
    "consumers"
  ],
  "min_confidence": "possible",
